        {title:"Characteristics to name in an answer",lead:"If asked for features, name a feature and explain the clue rather than listing labels alone.",items:[["Goal-oriented","All activity is directed toward defined objectives."],["Pervasive","Management is needed in every organisation and at all levels."],["Multidimensional","It manages work, people and operations."],["Continuous and dynamic","Functions recur and methods adapt as conditions change."],["Group and intangible","People act collectively; management is noticed through order, results and satisfaction."]]},{title:"Management as science, art and profession",lead:"Use a balanced conclusion: management has scientific knowledge and artistic application, but is not a fully regulated profession in the textbook account.",items:[["Science","It has an organised body of knowledge and principles developed from observation and experience. Human behaviour varies, so outcomes are not as exact or universally predictable as in pure sciences."],["Art","A manager applies knowledge personally and skillfully; practice, judgement and creativity help turn it into results."],["Profession: what fits","Management has a teachable body of knowledge and an increasingly recognised service role."],["Profession: what is incomplete","A manager need not hold a mandatory licence or degree; association membership is not compulsory; the textbook notes no statutory, profession-wide code. So management is not a full-fledged profession like law or medicine."],["Exam conclusion","Science supplies tested ideas; art adapts them to a situation. The two complement each other."]]},{title:"Coordination: the thread through management",lead:"Coordination consciously aligns interdependent effort; it is the essence of management, built into every function rather than a separate fifth or sixth function.",items:[["Integrates group effort","Combines different people's and departments' work around shared objectives."],["Creates unity of action","Keeps individual actions pointed toward the common purpose."],["Continuous","Begins in planning and continues as work is organised, staffed, directed and controlled."],["Pervasive; every manager's responsibility","Needed across levels and departments because their work depends on one another."],["Deliberate","Managers actively synchronise effort; goodwill alone does not ensure the work is aligned."]]}
